    Candidate Modules:
    - **dsp**: This module mainly corresponds to low-level digital signal processing capabilities, providing foundational algorithm support for upper-level transforms, spectra, filtering, and audio processing. It supports the Short-time Fourier transform, BFT/STFT-style transforms, spectrograms at different frequency scales, audio resampling, complex-spectrum phase extraction, and other basic processing.
- **feature**: This module is used to extract audio features from spectral, cepstral, and time-domain data. It mainly covers Spectral, XXCC, Deconv, Cepstrogram, Temporal, and FeatureExtractor functionality: Spectral computes various spectral features, XXCC extracts cepstral coefficients, Deconv performs spectral deconvolution, Temporal extracts time-domain features such as energy, RMS, and zero-crossing rate, and FeatureExtractor supports batch feature extraction.
- **filter_bank**: This module is mainly responsible for constructing and applying different types of spectral filter banks and auditory weights, used to generate spectral representations under different scales or perceptual models.
- **general**: This module is the core general algorithm layer of AudioFlux, centralizing major time-frequency transforms, spectral computation, basic audio I/O, and common utilities. It provides spectrogram generation as well as multiple time-frequency transforms, synchrosqueezing, reassignment algorithms, audio reading, writing, mono conversion, resampling, and other common capabilities.
    
